# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Credentials — never commit these
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.Renviron
.Rprofile.local

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# R and RStudio session files
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/
*.Rproj

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Quarto working files
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.quarto/
/_freeze/
# `quarto render` also renders README.md, landing an HTML copy in the project
# root that is no part of the site. The site itself is built into docs/.
/README.html
**/*.quarto_ipynb
pipeline_run.log
render.log

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Raw GBIF archives
#
# These are large and fully reproducible from the DOI recorded in
# data/run_metadata.rds, so they are not tracked. The download key IS tracked,
# so that a fresh clone re-uses the same DOI rather than minting a new one.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/data/gbif_download/*
!/data/gbif_download/download_key.txt

# GBIF archives anywhere under data/ (older runs left some at the top level).
/data/*.zip

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT ignored
#
# data/eu_directives_species.csv  — the annex list is a project input
# data/vernacular_cache.csv       — cache; avoids thousands of API calls on a
#                                   fresh clone
# data/iucn_cache.csv             — same, for IUCN Red List categories
# data/dataset_registry.csv       — same, for dataset and publisher titles
# data/gadm41_XKO.gpkg            — GADM 4.1 source for both layers below
# data/kosovo_boundary.gpkg       — national outline, GADM level 0
# data/kosovo_municipalities.gpkg — GADM level 2, used for coverage reporting
# data/kosovo_protected_areas.gpkg— Kosovo's slice of the EEA Nationally
#                                   designated areas inventory. Cached rather
#                                   than rebuilt, because building it reads a
#                                   1.7 GB European file over the network; the
#                                   cache is 700 kB and takes a minute to
#                                   regenerate if deleted
# data/run_metadata.rds           — required to render the report
# data_exports/                   — published outputs, served by GitHub Pages
# docs/                           — the rendered website itself
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
